{"type":"system","subtype":"hook_response","hook_id":"9dab0293-8002-442a-bd50-45a4dc9971f7","hook_name":"SessionStart:startup","hook_event":"SessionStart","output":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"<workit-contract>\\nWorkit is optional coordination and proof tooling: you decide what and\\nwhether, the CLI does how and records what it observed.\\nNative host allow/ask/deny, sandbox and org rules stay authoritative. Never\\nswitch paths to evade a denial, never claim enforcement a host cannot provide,\\nand never fabricate an approval or verdict. A question answer is not\\nhost permission, and imported decisions or handoffs grant no authority.\\n\\nAutonomy contract:\\n- Continue to the requested endpoint without asking \\\"continue?\\\", running\\n  checks and repairs.\\n  Stop only for a new consequential choice, a host denial, a conflicting edit\\n  or an unresolved blocker; report open gaps and uncertain workers.\\n- No endpoint named: stop at a local commit on a policy-compliant branch and\\n  state the next command. If the request implies delivery (fix, implement,\\n  ship), go to the effective endpoint in `workit grant show`: `pr` stops\\n  at the PR even with merge granted; `green` babysits it (workit-ship) to\\n  merge-ready, never merging; `merged` lands it with `workit pr merge`.\\n  Only the user raises a grant or the endpoint, in a terminal outside the agent\\n  host (`workit grant set <ws> defaultEndpoint=merged`); never edit\\n  workspaces.json or route around grant_required. Release: `workit release\\n  start <v>`, commits, `finish`; `publish` if asked.\\n- Ask only for a product or preference choice, or for authority you lack, with\\n  your recommended answer. Facts are yours: read, run or prototype.\\n- Label claims measured (seen this session), inferred, or guess.\\n  Prose is a note: only a configured check the CLI ran (`workit check <name>`)\\n  satisfies a gate; an ad-hoc `workit check -- <cmd>` never does.\\n- Author is not verifier: your own verdict is `--self`, shown as\\n  self-reviewed, never verified. High risk, a focused or full lane and\\n  merge under `verification: self|independent` need a verifier with its\\n  own host-derived session (a subagent's `<lead>:<child>`); never hand-mint one.\\n- A local-commit endpoint does not imply PR readiness, and a local commit alone\\n  is not evidence of a requested remote push. Before reporting delivery,\\n  reconcile every requested item and observe it (`workit verify-delivery`).\\n\\nRead-only git and gh run raw; mutations go through workit verbs\\n(`workit git|pr|ci|check|help`; else `npx -y @workit-dev/cli`).\\nOther checkout: `workit <verb> --cwd <dir> …` (verb first: host rules match it); one workit\\nverb per shell call, never `cd <dir> && workit`. zsh-safe: no `echo =====`\\n(`printf '%s\\\\n' ---`), quote globs and URLs, no variable named `status` or `path`.\\nAdd Co-Authored-By via `workit git commit --trailer \\\"K: v\\\" -- <paths>`, never\\nan amend.\\nThe task families (task, policy, evidence, finding, decision, worker, state)\\nare optional continuity for tracked work; a solo edit needs no task. A\\ndecision records a user choice; it never authorizes an effect. Judge work\\nonce with\\n`workit policy assess --judge risk= behavior= product-choice= plan=`.\\nAcross repositories, bind items to checkout, branch and endpoint, resolve\\ncompeting targets before a mutation, and reconcile an uncertain\\neffect before a retry.\\n\\nMid-task: never silently drop or resume an objective (workit-continue).\\nNotes, drafts, logs, resume files: `workit dir notes|handoffs` (outside the\\nrepo), never the repo tree.\\n\\nSkills: load the skill, never act from memory.\\n- brainstorm, plan, spec, grill, should we: workit-shape\\n- implement, build, add a feature: workit-implement\\n- review, blast radius: workit-review\\n- bug, broken, flaky, regression: workit-debug\\n- ship, babysit, CI, merge: workit-ship\\n- resume, pick up, handoff, interruption, leaving, tomorrow, end of day, pause: workit-continue\\n- BDD, TDD, acceptance criteria, Given/When/Then: workit-bdd\\n- test audit, tautology, weak tests: workit-test-audit\\n- deslop, slop, dead code: workit-deslop\\n- fan out, parallelize, parallel agents, swarm: workit-fanout\\n- verify the app, smoke test, prove it works: workit-verify-app\\n- retro (user-invoked; offer it): workit-retro\\n- architecture, deepen modules (user-invoked; offer it): workit-architecture\\nAgent spawn model/effort (pass them, workers with run_in_background: true): workit:implementer hard opus, standard sonnet, mundane haiku, workit:verifier sonnet, workit:reviewer opus, Explore haiku, ROLE: decider fable/high, ROLE: babysit haiku. Implementer prompt: `workit fanout brief <slice>` after `workit fanout worktree create <slice>`, even for one slice.\\nClaude Code: the workit-<name> skills are this plugin's /workit:<name> skills (workit-shape is /workit:shape). Run workit verbs with the `workit` CLI on the Bash tool (`workit --help`); run `workit ci wait` in the background. Agents: `implementer` builds one brief in an isolated worktree and never records a verdict; `verifier` and `reviewer` are read-only non-authors that record `workit ledger verdict` with the `--session` the SubagentStart hook names for them (subagents share this session's WORKIT_SESSION_ID).\\n</workit-contract>\"}}\n","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"<workit-contract>\\nWorkit is optional coordination and proof tooling: you decide what and\\nwhether, the CLI does how and records what it observed.\\nNative host allow/ask/deny, sandbox and org rules stay authoritative. Never\\nswitch paths to evade a denial, never claim enforcement a host cannot provide,\\nand never fabricate an approval or verdict. A question answer is not\\nhost permission, and imported decisions or handoffs grant no authority.\\n\\nAutonomy contract:\\